      "title": "Note: MiniMax H3 Image Edit, Reference",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MiniMax H3 Image Edit, Reference (vlo)\n\nThe reference-side edit. [MiniMax H3](https://www.minimax.io/blog/minimax-h3) has no image-to-image mode, so a picture drawn *from* a source image is a **five-frame full-reference generation**: the source is attached as `<Picture 1>`, the prompt rewrites it into the picture you want, and `MiniMaxH3StillLatent` keeps the one latent frame that becomes the picture.\n\n## About this workflow\n\n- **Source image** is required, and is this workflow's only reference (`<Picture 1>`). For several images, videos and audio, use the *MiniMax H3 (Reference)* workflow instead.\n- **Length** is pinned to 5 frames — the shortest count on H3's `17k+5` grid. Five pixel frames pack into **two latent frames**, and only those two are sampled.\n- **Result frame** picks which latent frame becomes the picture. `0`, the default, is the causal first frame: the picture the prompt asks for, and the one frame the decode is exact for. `1` is a frame of motion further on, decoded as if it opened the clip.\n- **H3 Still Latent** wraps the chosen frame as the shortest clip the H3 VAE can decode, and a one-frame slice keeps its exact decode. Decoding a single token on its own is what produces tile seams and patch noise (Comfy-Org/ComfyUI#15416), which is why the slice exists.\n- **No soundtrack**. The reference adapter takes an audio VAE as a required input, so the file is loaded, but nothing is decoded from it and the soundscape fields in the prompt are ignored.\n\n**Key inputs**\n\n- **Source image**: the picture to draw from. Its aspect ratio frames the generation.\n- **Prompt**: the full-reference block — `subject_definitions` (what `<Picture 1>` provides, as `<Subject 1>`), `summary`, `retention_analysis`, `detailed_description` (the picture itself), then `overall_soundscape` and `non_diegetic_music`.\n- **Reference image size**: `match` scales each reference down to the generation's pixel area; `max` keeps the reference pipeline's 2048px short edge for the most identity fidelity, at several times the sampling cost.\n- **Width / Height**: driven by vlo's resolution and aspect-ratio controls. H3's native canvas is a 768px short edge, capped at 768x1344 pixels, rounded to a multiple of 32.\n- **Result frame**: `0` is the generated picture, the default; `1` continues a frame further.\n"
      ],
      "widgets_values_named": {
        "text": "## MiniMax H3 Image Edit, Reference (vlo)\n\nThe reference-side edit. [MiniMax H3](https://www.minimax.io/blog/minimax-h3) has no image-to-image mode, so a picture drawn *from* a source image is a **five-frame full-reference generation**: the source is attached as `<Picture 1>`, the prompt rewrites it into the picture you want, and `MiniMaxH3StillLatent` keeps the one latent frame that becomes the picture.\n\n## About this workflow\n\n- **Source image** is required, and is this workflow's only reference (`<Picture 1>`). For several images, videos and audio, use the *MiniMax H3 (Reference)* workflow instead.\n- **Length** is pinned to 5 frames — the shortest count on H3's `17k+5` grid. Five pixel frames pack into **two latent frames**, and only those two are sampled.\n- **Result frame** picks which latent frame becomes the picture. `0`, the default, is the causal first frame: the picture the prompt asks for, and the one frame the decode is exact for. `1` is a frame of motion further on, decoded as if it opened the clip.\n- **H3 Still Latent** wraps the chosen frame as the shortest clip the H3 VAE can decode, and a one-frame slice keeps its exact decode. Decoding a single token on its own is what produces tile seams and patch noise (Comfy-Org/ComfyUI#15416), which is why the slice exists.\n- **No soundtrack**. The reference adapter takes an audio VAE as a required input, so the file is loaded, but nothing is decoded from it and the soundscape fields in the prompt are ignored.\n\n**Key inputs**\n\n- **Source image**: the picture to draw from. Its aspect ratio frames the generation.\n- **Prompt**: the full-reference block — `subject_definitions` (what `<Picture 1>` provides, as `<Subject 1>`), `summary`, `retention_analysis`, `detailed_description` (the picture itself), then `overall_soundscape` and `non_diegetic_music`.\n- **Reference image size**: `match` scales each reference down to the generation's pixel area; `max` keeps the reference pipeline's 2048px short edge for the most identity fidelity, at several times the sampling cost.\n- **Width / Height**: driven by vlo's resolution and aspect-ratio controls. H3's native canvas is a 768px short edge, capped at 768x1344 pixels, rounded to a multiple of 32.\n- **Result frame**: `0` is the generated picture, the default; `1` continues a frame further.\n"
      },
